        "U4",
        "C11"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "U4.27",
        "C11.1",
        "C11.2"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "VCC",
        "GND"
      ],
      "observed": "U4 pin 27 (VCOMH) is connected to the VCC rail, and C11 is connected between VCC and GND rather than between VCOMH and GND.",
      "expected": "The specification states that C11 is the 4.7 uF reservoir/filter capacitor from U4 VCOMH to GND; VCOMH should not be merged with the main VCC rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C11 (4.7 µF) — U4 VCOMH (charge-pump output) to GND, the output reservoir/filter cap"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"23\") (name \"VCC\") ... (node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"27\") (pinfunction \"VCOMH\") (pintype \"output\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"4\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C11 VCC 0 4.7u"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The SSD1306 charge-pump/bias output is shorted to the board VCC rail and its intended reservoir/filter capacitor is missing from that output, so the OLED panel bias voltage will be incorrect or the driver may be damaged.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files deviate from the specified OLED bias network: VCOMH is merged with VCC and C11 is a VCC bypass instead of the intended VCOMH-to-GND filter capacitor."
}

